---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="How this works, and why.">
  <article class="about">
    <div class="reading-container">
      <header class="about-header">
        <p class="kicker">Colophon</p>
        <h1 class="about-title">About this site</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <em>The Daily Paper</em> publishes one technical paper every morning,
          explained in enough depth that a working engineer could reimplement
          the core method from the explainer alone.
        </p>

        <h2>What's here</h2>
        <p>
          Each weekday, the pipeline pulls fresh papers from arXiv across
          roughly seven technical categories — machine learning, AI,
          computational linguistics, algorithms, computational finance, trading,
          and statistical ML — filters them by engagement signals like citation
          velocity and released code, and selects the single most interesting
          one against a curated interests file.
        </p>
        <p>
          That paper then gets a roughly 3,000-word reimplementation-grade
          write-up: the intuition, the full method with equations and
          pseudocode, a flow diagram, honest limitations, and practical notes
          for anyone wanting to build a prototype.
        </p>

        <h2>What's not here</h2>
        <p>
          No weekly roundups. No thread-style takes. No "this changes
          everything." If a paper isn't worth a thorough write-up, it isn't
          here.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's made</h2>
        <p>
          The pipeline is open-source. The paper selection uses a two-stage
          ranking: objective engagement signals reduce the daily firehose down
          to a shortlist, then Claude (an AI system built by Anthropic) picks
          the winner against the interests file. The explainer is then
          generated by Claude from the full paper text. Every page is a static
          HTML file — no tracking beyond server logs.
        </p>

        <h2>Quality caveats</h2>
        <p>
          These explainers are generated by a language model. They're reviewed
          only lightly — occasionally not at all — before publication. They
          will sometimes contain errors. They are a starting point for
          understanding a paper, not a replacement for reading the original.
          When something matters, go to the source.
        </p>

        <h2>Colophon</h2>
        <p>
          Typeset in <em>Fraunces</em> (display) and <em>Newsreader</em> (body)
          by Production Type / Adobe. Monospace is <em>JetBrains Mono</em>.
          Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>. Math renders via{' '}
          <a href="https://katex.org">KaTeX</a>. Diagrams via{' '}
          <a href="https://mermaid.js.org">Mermaid</a>.
        </p>

        <hr class="fine-rule" />

        <p class="about-outro">
          <a href="/">Return to the latest paper →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: var(--space-7); }

  .about-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }

  .about-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
  }

  .about-outro {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .about-outro a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
  }
</style>
